Hi everyone.

So here we go with the first real update and not a quick hotfix. What's inside?

- Fixed several issues with dialog boxes: freezing, not being able to close it, not working buttons, etc;
- Fixed several mistakes in Spanish localization (shout out to malkavi86);
- Fixed an issue with an engineer when he was able to go past a roadblock;
- Fixed a bug when after loading a saved game, emperor's attitude was different than before;
- Fixed textures of: temples, houses, prefecture and engineering post;
- Fixed several issues with incorrect saving of citizens' location/behavior;

+ Added market textures;
+ Added aqueducts textures;
+ Added roadblock textures;
+ Added cart pushers textures;
+ Added some missing parts to all localizations;
+ Changed a free for settlement area texture;
+ Map scrolling speed now depends on the map scale.

Be aware: unfortunatelly, your saved games will be lost after this update due to fixes made to the saving algorythm.

We hope you'll find this update useful. Have fun and keep us posted on new found bugs.

Hi guys.

A big, but still not that massive update is released:

- Objects drawing algorythm is rewritten, now people no longer get overlaid by ground tiles while they walk diagonally + big objects are no longer overlaid by ground when you remove/deconstruct them;
- Fixed a lot of mistakes in localizations;
- Fixed temples import from the original game for those of you who would like to play with original resources;
- Fixed fullscreen mode to properly support a chosen resolution;
- Fixed dust spreading algorythm;
- Fixed windowed mode, now it runs in the center of the screen by default;
- Fixed new textures for paved roads and a correct texture calculation algorythm;
- Fixed import settings;
- Fixed a bug with incorrect coordinates of a building while zoomed;
- Fixed warehouses filling bug: import from trading is now calculated in;
- Fixed scribes messages bug: they no longer appear empty;
+ Added a message when a mission is successfuly completed;
+ Added some modding drafts, mods details are loaded directly from the game folder;
+ Added new maps description format;
+ Added merchants assistants;
+ Added an option of stopping standalone working buildings.


Thank you for your support, don't stop reporting new found bugs. :)

